From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] virtdisk: a volume that is not a virtual disk (1528)

Windows answers GetStorageDependencyInformation for a file, volume or disk
that is not on a virtual disk with ERROR_VIRTDISK_NOT_VIRTUAL_DISK. Wine
said ERROR_SUCCESS with no entries. Microsoft 365 asks for the host volumes
of every document it opens; on that success Excel read a host volume name
from the empty buffer, passed it to wcsstr against "\\?\Volume{" and
faulted, then hung at "Opening - Excel" for any existing workbook (from
Recent or the command line). No volume under Wine is a virtual disk.

Gate: test/virtdiskdep-gate.sh.
Mutant: SG_MUTANT_VIRTDISK_EMPTY_SUCCESS (gate fails: file=0 vol=0).
virtdisk conformance unchanged (9 tests, 0 failures).

--- a/dlls/virtdisk/virtdisk_main.c
+++ b/dlls/virtdisk/virtdisk_main.c
@@ -40,9 +40,19 @@
     if (size < temp_size)
         return ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER;
 
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_VIRTDISK_EMPTY_SUCCESS
     info->NumberEntries = 0;
 
     return ERROR_SUCCESS;
+#else
+    /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 1528): no volume here is a virtual disk;
+     * Windows answers that for a file, volume or disk that is not on one.
+     * Success with no entries made Office read a host volume name from the
+     * empty buffer and fault while opening any existing workbook. */
+    if (!obj || obj == INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE) return ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE;
+    info->NumberEntries = 0;
+    return ERROR_VIRTDISK_NOT_VIRTUAL_DISK;
+#endif
 }
 
 DWORD WINAPI OpenVirtualDisk(VIRTUAL_STORAGE_TYPE *type, const WCHAR *path, VIRTUAL_DISK_ACCESS_MASK mask, OPEN_VIRTUAL_DISK_FLAG flags,
